[1.053973, "o", "t"]
[1.080429, "o", "\r\n"]
[1.713181, "o", "Initialized mnema project at ~/your-repository/.mnema\r\n  identity: mnid:af80cbcd9edfa5006d6131347e92b37e9606f7be15c429bcfc2f4ec9c3be0a36\r\n"]
[1.713364, "o", "  backup key: created and enrolled, private half at ~/.mnema/identity/backup/a50c03a0c375a5dd4bef205dfcad5a67ef70876616af3885e17bebb3889d4749.key\r\n"]
[1.713384, "o", "  Move that file off this machine: a backup left on this disk is lost with it.\r\n"]
[1.713652, "o", "Created AGENTS.md, with the mnema instructions.\r\n"]
[1.713669, "o", "Created .claude/rules/mnema-instructions.md, with the mnema instructions.\r\nCreated .github/instructions/mnema-instructions.instructions.md, with the mnema instructions.\r\nCreated .cursor/rules/mnema-instructions.mdc, with the mnema instructions.\r\n"]
[1.713721, "o", "Each holds the mnema instructions an agent host reads at the start of a session: when to call the mnema tools, and what never goes in the record. `mnema instructions --remove` takes them out.\r\n"]
[1.713735, "o", "\r\n"]
[1.713779, "o", "  mnema writes no other file of yours. In Claude Code the mnema plugin hands this record to\r\n  each session on its own. Without it, `mnema brief > MNEMA.md` puts what governs this\r\n"]
[1.713792, "o", "  project in a file of its own (the `>` replaces the whole of the file it names), and\r\n"]
[1.713813, "o", "  one line in a `CLAUDE.md` brings that file in (an `AGENTS.md` is read there only\r\n  where no `CLAUDE.md` exists):\r\n"]
[1.713825, "o", "    @MNEMA.md\r\n"]
[1.713987, "o", "\r\n  Commit `.mnema/` with the repository: the record travels with it, and every clone reads it.\r\n  Next: `mnema decision record <title> <rationale>`; `mnema status` shows where things stand.\r\n"]
[3.330761, "o", "\u001b[2m# write down a call, with the reasoning and what was turned down\u001b[0m\r\n"]
